CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ move-constructed member holds moved value: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
is not accessible
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.copy.ctor]/14-15: a defaulted move constructor direct-initializes
each base and non-static data member from the corresponding subobject of the
argument cast to an xvalue (static_cast<M&&>(other.m)); overload resolution on
that xvalue selects the member's move constructor.  A member whose copy
constructor is deleted but whose move constructor is usable must therefore be
moved, not copied.

Regression test for the fix that makes default_cpctor emit a move initializer
(static_cast<T&&>(ref.member)) for the move constructor, so the member's own
move constructor is selected.  assertion.1 checks the moved value is preserved
(non-vacuous: only holds if the move constructor body is actually elaborated
and the move runs); assertion.2 is a deliberately-wrong assertion that must
FAIL.  Before the fix this produced "member 'M::M(this, ...M&...)' is not
accessible" (the deleted copy constructor was selected) followed by a
CONVERSION ERROR that dropped the constructor body.
